==History of Gaimin Gladiators==
In 2022, Gaimin Gladiators signed the members of [[Team Tickles]] - [[dyrachyo]], [[BOOM]], [[Ace]], [[tOfu_(German player)|tOfu]], [[Seleri]], and coach [[ImmortalFaith]] after their promising run in [[Dota_Pro_Circuit/2021-22/1/Western_Europe/Division_I|Tour 1]] of the 2021-2022 WEU DPC. The newly sponsored team saw immediate success, beating [[Team Liquid]] in the [[Dota_Pro_Circuit/2021-22/1/Western_Europe/Regional_Final|WEU Regional Finals]], marking the beginning of a fierce rivalry. The Gladiators saw continued success, placing fourth at the [[ESL_One/Stockholm/2022|Stockholm Major]], and finishing middle of the pack at [[The International 2022]].

Before the 2022-2023 season, the team dropped mid player [[BOOM]] for [[Quinn]] and coach [[ImmortalFaith]] for [[Cy-]]. The re-vitalized Gaimin Gladiators proceeded to establish an international dominance in the first half of the season, winning the [[Lima_Major/2023|Lima Major]], [[Berlin Major]] and the [[Bali Major/2023|Bali Major]] back to back to back, each time defeating rivals [[Team Liquid]] in the finals. In doing so, Gaimin Gladiators became the first team to win three consecutive Majors since [[OG]] in 2016-2017.

===Withdrawal from The International 2025===
On August 22, 2025, having been invited directly to the event, Gaimin Gladiators withdrew from [[The International/2025|The International 2025]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/dota2ti/status/1958990135355482593|title=An update regarding The International.|author=Valve|date=2025-08-22}}</ref>  The organization released a statement, stating that the players attempted to compete independently of the organization, and due to rules governing roster changes, the organization was unable to field a lineup; the matter was also being discussed legally.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/GaiminGladiator/status/1959346161208213783|title=Official statement from the Gaimin Gladiators|author=Gaimin Gladiators|date=2025-08-23}}</ref>  This was also backed by owner Nick Cuccovillo.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/GGNickcvillo/status/1959008769385324993|title=I want to share that Gaimin Gladiators won’t be competing at TI this year. Some internal matters between the players and the organization made it impossible for us to move forward with a roster. For now, I can’t go into more detail as there are legal considerations involved, but|author=Nick Cuccovillo|date=2025-08-22}}</ref>  Midlaner [[Quinn]] also released a statement on behalf of the players, stating that the team was "ready, willing and able to compete in The International under the Gaimin Gladiators banner", but was prevented from doing so by the organization, who made the decision unilaterally to withdraw from The International.  He also cited that there were several issues under legal discussion.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ccncdota2/status/1959354086765003056|title=In light of the recent statement from Gaimin Gladiators about the  withdrawal from The International 2025 in Hamburg, we believe it  necessary to provide  some clarification. 1/2|author=Quinn|author-link=Quinn|date=2025-08-23}} {{!}} [https://x.com/ccncdota2/status/1959354086765003056 Part&nbsp;2] {{!}} [https://x.com/ccncdota2/status/1959355035290161631 Part&nbsp;3]</ref>

Nick Cuccovillo later responded to Quinn's statement, calling it misleading: After the team requested to play as independent players, Gaimin Gladiators informed Valve that they would not be able to field a roster for The International 2025, and the team did not engage with them nor agree to terms to settle.  As such, with no confidence that the players would remain with Gaimin Gladiators nor be in a position to represent them.  He also stated that not all information could be released, due to legal action.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/GGNickcvillo/status/1959496109966975093|title=Following the post from Quinn where he stated GG made a unilateral decision to withdraw from TI, his statement is misleading.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/ZjoFJ|author=Nick Cuccovillo|date=2025-08-24|archivedate=2025-08-24}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://rdy.gg/en/news/conflicting-statements-from-gaimin-gladiators-and-their-players-on-ti-2025-withdrawal|title=Conflicting statements from Gaimin Gladiators and their players on TI 2025 withdrawal|author=Andreea Esanu|publisher=rdy.gg|date=2025-05-24}}</ref>  This statement was criticized by [[Team Falcons]]' coach [[Aui_2000]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aui_2000/status/1959546015070966251|title=I can't believe this is the statement @GGNickcvillo is making while representing GG.|author=Aui 2000|date=2025-08-24}}</ref> [[Team Spirit]] manager [[Korb3n]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://cyber.sports.ru/dota2/1116874338-korb3n-prezident-gladiators-ne-xochet-nam-rasskazat-pochemu-igroki-res.html|title=Korb3n: «Президент Gladiators не хочет нам рассказать, почему игроки решили расторгнуть контракты в одностороннем порядке?»|trans_title=Korb3n: “The president of Gladiators doesn’t want to tell us why the players decided to terminate contracts unilaterally?”|language={{Flag|ru}} Russian|author=Илья Воробьёв|publisher=Кибер|date=2025-05-24}}</ref> and observer [[PimpmuckL]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/JJLiebig/status/1959583966987489284|title=This whole GG Dota drama is so damaging to the scene.  Taking away ti from players is really, really bad.  Having an org not get representation for the largest event and the main reason you sign them, also really bad and makes the ecosystem less attractive.  Either way, we all lose|author=JJ - PimpmuckL|date=2025-08-24}}</ref>

Former manager Oleg "[[rainbowsix:Jak2oO|Jak2oO]]" Porotnikov had heard inside sources that suggested that coach [[Cy-]] had been forced out of the team despite the players' desire to retain him, and speculated that this may have driven a wedge between the roster and the organization, leading to the players attempting to compete independently, but were stopped due to threats of legal action.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.si.com/esports/news/gaimin-gladiators-dota-2-team-drops-out-the-international|title=Top Dota 2 Team Drops Out of The International Two Weeks Before it Starts|publisher=Sports Illustrated|author=Cale Michael|date=2025-08-22}}</ref>

