'''Xtreme Gaming''' is a [[:Category:China|Chinese]] ''Dota 2'' team.

==History==
The team is founded by Yang Yiqing (the founder of [[Azure Ray]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://m.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_25428026|title=加快布局电竞产业、共同做强赛事经济！沈志栋会见大众国际董事兼总经理杨一清|author=今日相城|date=2023-11-25}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://weibo.com/6899345338/NujkiABD3|title=很多人好奇XG老板到底是什么来头|author=刀塔必知道|date=2023-11-26}}</ref> The organization later became the sole proprietorship of Ye Yi (叶亿).<ref name="xg 20231231">{{cite web|url=https://weibo.com/7720945580/4985117292103559|title=新年将至|author=XG|date=2023-12-31}}</ref>

In April 2023, Xtreme Gaming won the championship of [[Dota_Pro_Circuit/2023/2/China/Division_I|DPC CN 2023 Tour 2: Division I]].

In April 2024, Xtreme Gaming performed exceptionally well in multiple tournaments, successively winning championships at [[Games_of_the_Future/2024|Games of the Future 2024]], [[Elite_League/1|Elite League Season 1]], and [[Clavision/Snow_Ruyi/2024|Clavision: Snow Ruyi]], while also securing a runner-up finish at [[PGL/Wallachia/1|PGL Wallachia Season 1]].

In September 2025, Xtreme Gaming achieved a 4-0 record in the Swiss-system group stage of [[The_International/2025|The International 2025]], entering the Playoffs as the top-seeded team. They advanced all the way to the Grand Final, but unfortunately suffered a narrow 2-3 defeat against [[Team Falcons]], ultimately finishing as the runners-up.

